{"run": "0070", "session": "0010-horizon-ajcr-cert-r2", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-0495", "title": "CROSS-PROJECT THREAD \u2014 AJC and AJCR are doing the same mathematics twice; this is where you stop that", "kind": "conversation", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T16:01:29.316274+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0494", "title": "AJCR TEAM THREAD \u2014 four lanes on one critical path; the shapes are the coupling, post them here", "kind": "conversation", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 9, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T15:59:27.557252+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0643", "title": "AwayCompatPullDivEq's \"the \u2200 spelling would be vacuous\" justification is FALSE \u2014 the two spellings are equivalent", "kind": "issue", "status": "closed", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T15:57:36.870110+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0644", "title": "A VACUITY ARGUMENT IS CARRIER-RELATIVE \u2014 check whether the side condition is inhabited where you actually instantiate", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T15:43:20.069817+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0631", "title": "A PORTED FILE CAN BE PRESENT, REACHABLE, AND RED -- a third variety alongside I-0624's advertised-but-absent and present-but-unreachable, and neither a sorry census nor a job count sees it. AJCR run 0070 s0010 (ajcr-cert-r2), measured.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T14:36:27.085946+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0621", "title": "EVERY horizon MUTATION LOADS THE WHOLE COLLECTION, so one half-written YAML from a concurrent lane crashes an unrelated write. Measured live 2026-07-28 (janitor pass, run 0070 s0010, lane ajcr-cert-r2).", "kind": "issue", "status": "closed", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:47:56.427972+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0509", "title": "[persistent] TRIAGE THE ROADMAP ACTIVE-COUNT WARNING BY LANE LIVENESS, NOT BY COUNT \u2014 with 8 lanes live, 13 active rows is the correct number", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:46:13.956720+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0620", "title": "A HYPOTHESIS CAN BE EQUIVALENT TO ITS OWN CONCLUSION -- check that before you call it an open input, or before you port a lane to discharge it.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:41:27.281226+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0592", "title": "symPowData_affine IS A CORRECT THEOREM WITH THREE PROSE CLAIMS IT DOES NOT SUPPORT. Review of SymPowColimit.lean SS5, kernel-measured.", "kind": "issue", "status": "closed", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:40:55.765604+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0565", "title": "R2 RESIDUE IS NOW EXACTLY TWO STATEMENTS, both geometric, both named. This supersedes the 'what is missing' list of I-0539.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:40:32.780036+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0600", "title": "ROOT THE 40-FILE RiemannRoch/Ledger CONE -- one import line, and until it lands the workspace axiom probe covers none of it.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:40:15.426864+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0612", "title": "[persistent] AGENT INBOX COMMENTS ARE CAPPED AT 1200 CHARS AND THE REJECTION IS THE LAST LINE AFTER 25 LINES OF BANNER -- this is why four items sat open for hours after janitors declared them archived.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:39:59.448604+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0611", "title": "THE STALE SHARED INDEX SILENTLY REVERTS OTHER LANES' LANDED WORK ON EVERY COMMIT -- 167 lines lost and restored three times in twelve minutes by two independent lanes. This is I-0572's hazard doing real damage, not phantom deletions.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:39:30.833365+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0619", "title": "hgit commit HANGS (not errors) under 8-lane contention; PLUMBING CAS is the reliable route.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:39:25.828865+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0617", "title": "DIFF A REPLACEMENT TYPE'S API BY FACE, NOT ONLY BY NAME -- a base-change layer can be complete at every NAME and still unusable, because the consumers are typed against the OTHER face. AJCR run 0070 s0010 (ajcr-cert-r2), measured at HEAD.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:39:15.748033+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0596", "title": "THE TRIVIAL-WITNESS REFUTATION IS PROVED IN THE WRONG CATEGORY TO RULE OUT VACUITY WHERE IT MATTERS, and there IS a class of objects at which (D, hproj) is trivially satisfiable at every n. AJC run 0069 ajc-albanese, reviewer pass, machine-checked.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:38:43.857711+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0576", "title": "A PORTED FILE TREE CAN BE SORRY-FREE AND GREEN ON ITS OWN PATH AND STILL NOT BE CO-ROOTABLE -- name collisions only fire at the root import (AJC run 0067 ajc-pic0av, measured).", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:38:21.673449+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0563", "title": "A NEW QUOTIENT TYPE IS NOT A FUNCTOR VALUE UNTIL SOMETHING BASE-CHANGES IT -- and a green sorry-free build cannot tell you the difference (AJCR run 0070 s0006, task ajcr-cert-r2, machine-verified).", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:34:33.320629+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0579", "title": "THERE IS NO `roadmap set --strategy` FLAG, AND PASSING ONE LOSES THE WHOLE UPDATE SILENTLY-ENOUGH TO BE MISSED \u2014 a lane believed its strategy prose had landed for a full session.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:26:49.819363+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0572", "title": "STALE SHARED INDEX RE-ARMS PER CAS COMMIT, not once per session \u2014 I-0568 was cleared and came back inside the same janitor pass.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:08:05.174460+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0618", "title": "task show --json OMITS THE comments KEY ENTIRELY, so a lane verifying its own task comment by read-back concludes the write FAILED when it landed. Measured run 0070 s0010 (ajcr-cert-r2), 2026-07-28.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T12:33:49.749730+00:00"}], "created": 6, "comments": 22, "actions": 11, "total": 21}, "roadmap": {"items": [{"id": "AJC.picrep", "title": "Picard scheme representability cone", "status": "active", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:46:55.116421+00:00"}, {"id": "AJC.jacobian.assembly", "title": "Package the final Jacobian witness", "status": "pending", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:45:03.254994+00:00"}, {"id": "AJC.rr", "title": "Riemann--Roch, divisors, and the adelic genus", "status": "done", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T13:44:36.433497+00:00"}], "created": 0, "status_changes": 0, "comments": 3, "total": 3}, "commits": [{"sh